   {
    "chapter": "THE ORDER"
   },
   {
    "q": "WHOSE ORDER IS IT",
    "a": "ATTRIBUTED TO SHAO YONG 邵雍,\nELEVENTH CENTURY.",
    "show": {
     "diagram": {
      "kind": "overview"
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "q": "HOW",
    "a": "EACH PATTERN BRANCHES INTO TWO.\nEACH STAGE ADDS A LINE.\nSIX STAGES: 64 PATTERNS.",
    "show": {
     "diagram": {
      "kind": "tree",
      "at": 1,
      "morph": 7.5
     },
     "hold": 9
    }
   },
   {
    "q": "A FRIEND'S VERDICT",
    "a": "CHENG HAO 程顥:\n\"JUST THE DOUBLING METHOD.\"\n加一倍法",
    "show": {
     "diagram": {
      "kind": "tree",
      "at": -10,
      "dim": 0.35
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "q": "THE SQUARE",
    "a": "THE SAME 64 AS A SQUARE.\nA TRIGRAM IS THREE LINES.\nROWS SHARE THE LOWER ONE,\nCOLUMNS THE UPPER.",
    "show": {
     "diagram": {
      "kind": "square",
      "at": 3,
      "row": 2,
      "col": 5
     },
     "hold": 7
    }
   },
   {
    "chapter": "WHAT IT MEANT"
   },
   {
    "q": "DID LEIBNIZ GET BINARY HERE",
    "a": "NO. HE HAD IT BY 1679.\nSHAO YONG DID NOT USE THESE\nPATTERNS AS NUMERALS.\nLEIBNIZ SAW CONFIRMATION.",
    "show": {
     "diagram": {
      "kind": "pair"
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "q": "WHAT DID LEIBNIZ SAY",
    "a": "\"PERHAPS THE MOST ANCIENT\nMONUMENT OF SCIENCE.\"",
    "show": {
     "plate": {
      "zoom": [
       1,
       1.08
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   {
